{"kind":"charness.bounded_review.v1","lens":"Preflight auth-copy cleanup and claim accuracy","verdict":"block","target_observations":null,"findings":[{"id":"R-001","severity":"high","summary":"The copied auth file can survive a failure during preflight environment setup.","evidence":["In `_run_brief_critique`, `private_review_environment(...)` runs before the `try/finally`; the `finally` only covers `_execute_codex` and later paths.","`private_review_environment` opens the destination auth file before `shutil.copyfileobj`; an I/O error during the copy can leave a partial or complete file behind without reaching `discard_review_auth`.","The failure test raises from the mocked `_execute_codex`, so it does not cover an exception during environment setup."],"action":"Put private environment setup under the cleanup `try/finally` and add a setup-failure test that leaves a destination file before raising."}],"counterweight_triage":[{"concern":"Auth deletion might break a normal or failed Codex preflight.","bin":"not-blocking","disposition":"The `finally` runs after `_execute_codex` returns or raises, and the tests assert the copy exists during review and is gone after success and an execution exception."},{"concern":"Another Claude lane may read a finished preflight copy under `/tmp` or `/var/tmp`.","bin":"not-blocking","disposition":"After the tested success path the copy is deleted; the cross-lane probes fail to read its path in both layouts. The code and docs also disclose that another lane can read it while the preflight is running."},{"concern":"Changed notes and docs overstate other listed behaviors.","bin":"not-blocking","disposition":"The private-Git status caveat, Claude TMPDIR location, final-output observation, and writable-grant exclusions match the supplied implementations."}],"next_move":"Close the environment-setup cleanup gap and review that path before accepting the claim that the auth copy is deleted on every preflight exit path.","non_claims":["I reviewed the supplied semantic payload; I did not execute tests or bubblewrap probes.","The selected cross-lane tests establish unreadability after completion in their layouts, not direct live cross-lane access during a running preflight."]}
